@*
    The chart: a plain SVG polyline per series, drawn from geometry that was
    computed before this component was reached.

    Everything here came out of TelemetryChart, which is a pure function of the
    result - including each legend reading, already formatted with the entry's
    unit, and each palette class, handed out from a fixed table. This component
    allocates nothing per frame: it emits strings the model composed, and it
    walks its list by index rather than with foreach, because foreach over an
    IReadOnlyList<T> boxes the backing array's enumerator on every render and a
    metrics panel re-renders on every refresh.

    Neither loop uses @key. A legend label is composed from label VALUES and is
    capped at three of them, so two series agreeing on the first three but
    differing in a fourth would key identically - and Blazor throws on duplicate
    sibling keys, which on a server circuit tears down the whole connection
    rather than just this panel. Positional diffing is correct here anyway: the
    plot array is rebuilt wholesale whenever the result changes, and a polyline
    holds no state worth preserving across a reorder.

    It carries no width. The SVG scales itself to whatever box the stylesheet
    gives it, so a phone gets a smaller chart rather than a horizontally
    scrolling one, and there is no media query and no measurement anywhere in
    this package (epic decision D7).
*@

<figure class="lxt-chart">
    @if (Chart.IsEmpty)
    {
        <figcaption class="lxt-muted">@EmptyText</figcaption>
    }
    else
    {
        <svg class="lxt-plot"
             viewBox="@TelemetryChart.ViewBox"
             preserveAspectRatio="none"
             role="img"
             aria-label="@Label">
            @for (var i = 0; i < Chart.Plots.Count; i++)
            {
                var plot = Chart.Plots[i];
                @if (!plot.IsEmpty)
                {
                    <polyline class="@TelemetryPalette.SeriesClass(plot.PaletteIndex)"
                              points="@plot.Points" />
                }
            }
        </svg>

        <figcaption class="lxt-legend">
            <ul class="lxt-legend-items">
                @for (var i = 0; i < Chart.Plots.Count; i++)
                {
                    var plot = Chart.Plots[i];
                    <li class="lxt-legend-item">
                        <span class="@TelemetryPalette.SwatchClass(plot.PaletteIndex)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="lxt-legend-label">@plot.Label</span>
                        <span class="lxt-legend-value">@plot.Reading</span>
                    </li>
                }
            </ul>

            @if (Chart.IsTruncated)
            {
                <p class="lxt-muted" role="status">
                    Showing @Chart.Plots.Count of @Chart.TotalSeries series. Narrow the tree filter to see the rest.
                </p>
            }
        </figcaption>
    }
</figure>

@code {
    /// <summary>The geometry to draw, already computed from the result.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public TelemetryChart Chart { get; set; } = TelemetryChart.Empty;

    /// <summary>The accessible name of the plot, taken from the entry's server-authored title.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "Telemetry chart";

    /// <summary>What to say when there is nothing to draw.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string EmptyText { get; set; } = "No series matched.";
}
